  "rationale": "This item asks which patient does not require opioid dose reduction. Chronic opioid use implies tolerance, unlike the other options which increase opioid sensitivity or toxicity risk.",
  "optionExplanations": {
    "A": "Renal or liver failure can reduce opioid clearance and increase toxicity risk, so dose reduction is usually needed.",
    "B": "Neonates have immature metabolism and increased sensitivity to opioids, so reduced dosing is needed.",
    "C": "Head injury or reduced consciousness increases the risk of opioid-related respiratory depression and masking neurological deterioration.",
    "D": "Conditions that increase respiratory risk warrant caution and often reduced opioid dosing with close monitoring.",
    "E": "Chronic opioid use usually indicates tolerance; these patients do not typically need a reduced dose and may need a higher dose for analgesia."
  },
